; expect 42
; A module may keep a declaration to itself. `pub` and an import's
; name list decide which BARE NAMES are visible, not which
; declarations exist, and those are two different things that used to
; share one `if` in `resolveDeclsPhase`.
;
; With them conflated, a module with a private helper was a module
; nobody could import: its public bodies were spliced into the program
; and the declarations they call were dropped, so `axiom check` on the
; IMPORTING file reported `AX3001 undefined variable` at the imported
; file's own lines. `Priv.ax` has three such declarations - a private
; `data`, a private function matching on it, and a private helper -
; and under the old rule this file did not compile at all.
;
; Three terms, and each fails differently if the rule is wrong:
;
;   (quad 2)       18 - the module's public body calling its OWN
;                       private `scale`, twice. If a carried private
;                       name resolves outward instead of locally this
;                       is 4, because THIS file defines `scale` too.
;                       That is the silent half of the old defect:
;                       the dropped declaration left the bare slot
;                       free, the importer's definition claimed it,
;                       and the module's own call landed on it - at
;                       exit 0, with no diagnostic from any pass.
;   (scale 2)       3 - this file's own reference to its own
;                       definition, which must not have moved.
;   (roundTrip 5)   5 - a private `data`, its constructor and a
;                       private function that matches on it, all
;                       reached from a public body. This is the term
;                       that fails if only functions were carried and
;                       types were left behind.
(import Priv)

(:: scale (-> Int Int))

(fn (scale n) (+ n 1))

(:: main Int)

(fn (main)
  (if (== (+ (+ (quad 2) (scale 2)) (roundTrip 5)) 26)
    42
    1
  )
)
